Material for help2man(1), which generates the disparPDF manual page from
"disparPDF --help" and "disparPDF --version" plus the sections below.

[NAME]
disparPDF \- compare two PDF files textually or visually

[>DESCRIPTION]
.PP
By default the comparison is of the words on each pair of pages, but
comparing character by character is also supported (e.g., for
logographic languages).  And there's also support for comparing the
pages by appearance (for example, if a diagram is changed or if a
paragraph is reformatted, or a font changed).  It is also possible to
compare particular pages or page ranges, and to pair each page of one
file with a page further on in the other, for when pages have been
inserted or removed.
.PP
The differences can be saved as a PDF file, with the pages side by side
and the differences highlighted.
.PP
With
.BR \-\-batch ,
or as
.BR disparPDFc (1),
the files are compared without a window, which needs no display.

[EXAMPLES]
Compare the words of two files:
.PP
.RS
disparPDF old.pdf new.pdf
.RE
.PP
Compare their appearance without a window, saving the pages that differ
to
.IR changes.pdf ,
and printing the result code and a description:
.PP
.RS
disparPDF \-\-batch \-\-outType=1 \-\-pdfdiff=changes.pdf old.pdf new.pdf
.RE

[FILES]
.TP
.I ~/.config/disparPDF/disparPDF.conf
Settings of the window (layout, zoom, margins, highlighting, etc.).
Batch mode does not use them; see
.BR \-\-settings .

[AUTHORS]
DiffPDF was written by Mark Summerfield (2008\(en2013).  ConfrontaPDF,
which added batch mode, is a fork of it by Luca Bellonda (2015), and
disparPDF is a port of that to Qt\~6 by Yuwsuke Kieda (2026).

[REPORTING BUGS]
https://github.com/yuw/disparPDF/issues

[SEE ALSO]
.BR disparPDFc (1),
.BR diff (1)
.PP
The full documentation is available from the program's Help button
(F1).
